  "body": "### Summary\nAs the PO, I want to be sure the form leaks no data and resists abuse before it opens.\n\n### Scope\n- Read-only review of code and configuration: injection, storage of the pseudo, logs, HTTP headers, anti-abuse, match with the UX-06 data notice.\n- Then the PO deploys on the VPS with restricted access for the five-tester trial.\n\n### Deliverable\nReview report with findings; test URL.\n\n### Blocked by\n#634 (UX-10); the sub-domain choice.\n\n### Model and review\nFable review (read-only); deployment done or confirmed by the PO. Brief: `docs/ux/cadrage-agents-questionnaire.md` §3, UX-11.\n\nTracked on #628.\n\n### Before you start\n\nRead, in order: `AGENTS.md`, `docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md`, `docs/agents/LESSONS.md`, then `docs/ux/README.md`. The UX documents are in French. Until the docs PR is merged into `dev-swift`, read them on branch `docs/ux-questionnaire`.\n\nRules: no proposal the PO classed **Non** may appear in the survey (`docs/ux/tri-m5-decisions.md` §3.5 and §4.7). The reader keeps the WebView: the survey only shows improvements possible with it. Stop and report if an instruction contradicts the plan.\n\n---\n_Opened with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code) for the PO (Bruno), 2026-11-07._\n\n\n",
